--TEST--
Ordering two values of a built-in class that has no order is `E0411`, and its help names what to compare. A program cannot give a built-in class a `compareTo`, so the help never says to write one
--FILE--
<?nvs
Core\Regex\Pattern $first = Core\Regex::compile('a+');
Core\Regex\Pattern $second = Core\Regex::compile('b+');
echo $first < $second ? "earlier\n" : "later\n";

Core\Time\Zone $here = Core\Time\Zone::of('UTC');
Core\Time\Zone $there = Core\Time\Zone::of('Europe/Berlin');
echo $here < $there ? "before\n" : "after\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0411]: `Core\Regex\Pattern` does not implement `Comparable`; ordering two objects with `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`/`<=>` requires it
%A
  = help: `Core\Regex\Pattern` is a built-in class, and it has no order. Compare a value one of its methods returns, such as a number or a string
%A
error[E0411]: `Core\Time\Zone` does not implement `Comparable`; ordering two objects with `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`/`<=>` requires it
%A
  = help: `Core\Time\Zone` is a built-in class, and it has no order. Compare a value one of its methods returns, such as a number or a string
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
